c-final
boot seed 20261117 clock 1763400000 updates area
rng 51909 3b8e3587
step 1 "@connect d"
rng 51909 3b8e3587
step 2 "Delver"
out d "\n\r\n\rTHIS IS A MUD BASED ON.....\n\r\n\r                                ROM Version 2.4 beta\n\r\n\r               Original DikuMUD by Hans Staerfeldt, Katja Nyboe,\n\r               Tom Madsen, Michael Seifert, and Sebastian Hammer\n\r               Based on MERC 2.1 code by Hatchet, Furey, and Kahn\n\r               ROM 2.4 copyright (c) 1993-1998 Russ Taylor\n\r\n\rBy what name do you wish to be known? Password: \xff\xfb\x01"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 3 "psswrd"
out d "\n\r\xff\xfc\x01* You are responsible for knowing the rules (type 'rules').  Ignorance of \n\r  the rules is no excuse.\n\r* Important commands: help, commands, news, notes\n\r* Use the delete command to erase unwanted characters\n\r  \n\r[Hit Return to continue]\n\r"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 4 "@return"
out d "\n\rWelcome to Charm.  Please don't feed the mobiles!\n\rOn the Concourse\n\r  The concourse continues its path around the city.  The southern gates of the\n\rcity are west of here, and park road lies north.  The northeastern corner of\n\rthe city wall is east.\n\r\nNum          Name Unread Description\n\r==== ============ ====== =============================\n\r( 1)      General [   0] General discussion\n\r( 2)        Ideas [   0] Suggestion for improvement\n\r( 3)     Announce [   0] Announcements from Immortals\n\r( 4)         Bugs [   0] Typos, bugs, errors\n\r( 5)     Personal [   0] Personal messages\n\r\n\rYou current board is General.\n\rYou can both read and write on this board.\n\r\n\r<29hp 102m 106mv> \xff\xf9"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 5 "asave 48"
out d "\n\r<29hp 102m 106mv> \xff\xf9"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 6 "@file olcsave.are"
file olcsave.are "#AREADATA\nName OLC save tests~\nBuilders Planner Delver~\nVNUMs 30200 31299\nCredits { 1  5} Charm   OLC save tests~\nSecurity 3\nEnd\n\n\n\n#MOBILES\n#30200\nkeeper shopkeeper~\nthe keeper~\nThe keeper of the test shop stands here.\n~\nShe sells a little of everything.\n~\ndwarf~\nABG 0 500 7\n10 2 2d6+10 10d10+-5 1d8+2 punch\n-1 -15 -10 25\nEF 0 LQ R\nstand stand female 100\nAHV ABCDEFGHIJK medium unknown\nF aff J\nF for M\nM GREET 30201 100~\nM SPEECH 30200 hello~\n#30201\ngolem clay~\na clay golem~\nA clay golem stands here, very still.\n~\n~\nhuman~\nAQ 0 -1000 0\n20 0 5d5+100 1d1+0 3d3+3 beating\n-5 -5 -5 -5\n0 0 0 0\nsleep rest male 0\nAHMV ABCDEFGHIJK large unknown\n#31224\ntwin keeper~\nthe twin keeper~\nThe keeper's twin stands here, in the same hash chain as the keeper.\n~\n~\nhuman~\nAB 0 0 0\n5 0 1d1+1 1d1+1 1d1+1 punch\n0 0 0 0\n0 0 0 0\nstand stand male 0\nAHMV ABCDEFGHIJK medium unknown\n#0\n\n\n\n#OBJECTS\n#30200\nwaterskin skin~\na waterskin~\nA waterskin lies here.~\nleather~\ndrink 0 AO\n20 10 'water' 0 0\n1 2 10 P\n#30201\nchest~\na wooden chest~\nA wooden chest stands in the corner.~\nwood~\ncontainer 0 A\n50 ABC 30206 10 50\n5 20 100 G\nE\nchest wooden~\nThe chest has a brass lock.\n~\n#30202\nblade sword~\na test blade~\nA test blade lies on the floor.~\nsteel~\nweapon GH AN\nsword 2 6 slash DF\n10 8 500 A\nA\n1 1\nF\nV 0 0 G\nF\nR 0 0 F\nF\nI 0 0 E\nF\nA 0 0 J\nA\n19 -1\nA\n18 2\n#30203\npotion red~\na red potion~\nA red potion has been left here.~\nglass~\npotion 0 AO\n0 'cure light' 'bless' '' ''\n3 1 20 W\n#30204\nstaff oak~\nan oak staff~\nAn oak staff leans against the wall.~\noak~\nstaff 0 AO\n20 5 5 'fireball' 0\n15 4 900 D\n#30205\nrock~\na rock~\nA plain rock.~\nstone~\ntrash 0 A\nABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdef ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcde 0 B 0\n0 1 0 B\n#30206\nkey brass~\na brass key~\nA brass key.~\nbrass~\nkey 0 A\n0 0 0 0 0\n0 1 0 R\n#31224\npebble~\na pebble~\nA pebble, in the same hash chain as the waterskin.~\nstone~\ntrash 0 A\n0 0 0 0 0\n0 1 0 P\n#0\n\n\n\n#ROOMS\n#31224\nThe Twin Room~\nA room in the same hash chain as the test shop.\n~\n0 0 0\nD0\nBack to the shop.\n~\n~\n0 0 30200\nD1\nA door that starts open: there's no reset to close it.\n~\ndoor~\n0 0 30201\nS\n#30200\nThe Test Shop~\nA small shop where things are tested.\n   Shelves line the walls.\n~\n0 12 0\nE\nshelves shelf~\nDusty shelves.\n~\nD0\nA plain way north.\n~\n~\n0 0 30201\nD1\nA wooden door.\n~\ndoor wooden~\n1 30206 30201\nD2\nA pickproof door.\n~\ndoor~\n2 0 30201\nD3\nA door nothing passes.\n~\ndoor~\n3 0 30201\nD4\nA trapdoor above.\n~\ntrapdoor~\n4 30206 30201\nD5\nDown to the temple.\n~\n~\n0 -1 3001\nM 120 H 80\nO Planner~\nS\n#30201\nThe Back Room~\nThe back room of the test shop.\n~\n0 0 1\nD2\nBack to the shop.\n~\n~\n0 0 30200\nM 100 H 50\nC rom~\nS\n#30202\nA Room With No Way Out~\nNothing here.\n~\n0 4 1\nS\n#0\n\n\n\n#SPECIALS\nM 31224 spec_janitor\nM 30201 spec_cast_mage\nS\n\n\n\n#RESETS\nD 0 30200 1 2\nD 0 30200 4 1\nM 0 31224 1 31224 1 Load the twin keeper\nO 0 31224 0 31224 A pebble loaded to The Twin Room\nM 0 30200 1 30200 1 Load the keeper\nG 0 30203 0 A red potion is given to the keeper\nE 0 30202 0 16 A test blade is loaded wielded of the keeper\nO 0 30201 0 30200 A wooden chest loaded to The Test Shop\nP 0 30205 1 30201 1 A rock put inside a rock\nM 0 30201 1 30201 1 Load a clay golem\nE 0 30204 0 17 An oak staff is loaded held in the hands of a clay golem\nR 0 30201 3 Randomize The Back Room\nS\n\n\n\n#SHOPS\n31224 1 0 0 0 0 100 100 0 23\n30200 5 10 0 0 0 120 80 6 22\n0\n\n\n\n#MOBPROGS\n#30200\nsay Hello, $n.\n~\n#30201\nsmile $n\n~\n#0\n\n#HELPS\n0 OLCSAVE~\nA help in an area file, which asave writes back with the area.\n~\n\n-1 $~\n\n#$\n"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 7 "@connect b"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 8 "Planner"
out b "\n\r\n\rTHIS IS A MUD BASED ON.....\n\r\n\r                                ROM Version 2.4 beta\n\r\n\r               Original DikuMUD by Hans Staerfeldt, Katja Nyboe,\n\r               Tom Madsen, Michael Seifert, and Sebastian Hammer\n\r               Based on MERC 2.1 code by Hatchet, Furey, and Kahn\n\r               ROM 2.4 copyright (c) 1993-1998 Russ Taylor\n\r\n\rBy what name do you wish to be known? Password: \xff\xfb\x01"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 9 "smoke123"
out b "\n\r\xff\xfc\x01Welcome Immortal!\n\r\n\rYou are responsible for following the laws of immortal behavior. These can\n\rbe found by typing 'help laws' or 'help commandments'.\n\r\n\r* Excessive loading is not allowed, and is grounds for deletion.\n\r\n\r* Asking for promotion is grounds for instant deletion.\n\r\n\r* Type 'help jobs' to get some idea of what you should be doing.\n\r\n\r [Hit Return to continue]\n\r"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 10 "@return"
out b "\n\r* You are responsible for knowing the rules (type 'rules').  Ignorance of \n\r  the rules is no excuse.\n\r* Important commands: help, commands, news, notes\n\r* Use the delete command to erase unwanted characters\n\r  \n\r[Hit Return to continue]\n\r"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 11 "@return"
out b "\n\rWelcome to Charm.  Please don't feed the mobiles!\n\rThe Temple Of Mota [Room 3001]\n\r  You are in the southern end of the temple hall in the Temple of Mota.\n\rThe temple has been constructed from giant marble blocks, eternal in\n\rappearance, and most of the walls are covered by ancient wall paintings\n\rpicturing gods, giants and peasants.\n\r   Large steps lead down through the grand temple gate, descending the huge\n\rmound upon which the temple is built and ends on the temple square below.\n\r   Equally large steps lead UP through a small door into the ENTRANCE to MUD \n\rSCHOOL.  (type 'up' to go to MUD SCHOOL.)  A small plaque is on this wall.\n\rHassan is here, waiting to dispense some justice.\n\r\nNum          Name Unread Description\n\r==== ============ ====== =============================\n\r( 1)      General [   0] General discussion\n\r( 2)        Ideas [   0] Suggestion for improvement\n\r( 3)     Announce [   0] Announcements from Immortals\n\r( 4)         Bugs [   0] Typos, bugs, errors\n\r( 5)     Personal [   0] Personal messages\n\r\n\rYou current board is General.\n\rYou can both read and write on this board.\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 12 "asave world"
out b "You saved the world.\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9"
rng 51929 534cb46e
